text_en:
The definitions of the terms as used in this Act shall be as follows:
The term "telecommunications" means transmission or reception of code, words, sound or image through wired, wireless, optic, and other electro-magnetic processes;
The term "telecommunications facilities and equipment" means machinery, appliances, lines for telecommunications, and other facilities necessary for telecommunications;
The term "telecommunications line facilities and equipment" means the facilities and equipment which constitute communications channels between sending and receiving points for telecommunications among the telecommunications facilities and equipment, and the transmission and line facilities and equipment, with the exchange facilities installed as one body of the transmission and line facilities, and all facilities attached thereto;
The term "telecommunications business facilities and equipment" means the telecommunications facilities and equipment to be provided for telecommunications businesses;
The term "private telecommunications facilities and equipment" means the telecommunications facilities and equipment other than the telecommunications business facilities and equipment, installed by an individual to be used for his own telecommunications;
The term "telecommunications equipment" means apparatus, machinery, parts or line equipments, etc. used by the telecommunications facilities and equipment;
The term "telecommunications service" means services that mediate a third party's communication through the telecommunications facilities and equipment or to provide the telecommunications facilities and equipment for the third party's telecommunications;
The term "telecommunications business" means a business that provides telecommunications services.

